{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1527705714,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MzI3Mjk1OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-393272958"},"message":"I believe that it is a feature... If dataset is known and relative path, but not starting with curdir or pardir, then from top of the dataset, otherwise from current directory.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527705937,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MzI3NDE3MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-393274170"},"message":"Yes, it is a feature.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527705937,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTY1NDMwODc2OQ=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1527706228,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MzI3NTc1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-393275759"},"message":"Eh, a feature that makes \"this\" different than \"./this\"? IMO there shouldn't be a magical distinction between the two.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527706432,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MzI3NjgyOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-393276829"},"message":"Ah, I misread this. I read \"not resolved wrt relative path, but relative path to dataset\".\n\nMaybe a good time to write down a convention to stick to (ping #1819)","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527706432,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEzOlJlb3BlbmVkRXZlbnQxNjU0MzI2Mzk4"},"status":1},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1527715148,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MzMyMjk0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-393322948"},"message":"Yes, we need to document the convention, or get away from it (echoing @kyleam displease with it, and original use case where passed directory is just curdir ie .) but then there would be no way to specify \"file in the current directory\" while working with dataset's methods.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528181485,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NDYwMDg4Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-394600887"},"message":"I thought to fix this such that `./path` is equivalent to `path`, but it seems more fundamental change is desired. So far I was under the impression that \"specify 'file in the current directory' while working with dataset's methods\" is not a frequent use case, as we only work with absolute paths internally and generally produce portable code that uses the location of a dataset as *the* reference and not some PWD in some relation to a dataset.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1528205020,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NDcwNzE3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-394707179"},"message":"\u003e I thought to fix this such that ./path is equivalent to path, but it seems more fundamental change is desired.\n\nThat was in response to @yarikoptic's comment, but FTR your initial thought would cover what I had in mind, but I don't have a good grasp of the path handling, so I'm probably missing the deeper issues.\n\n\u003e So far I was under the impression that \"specify 'file in the current directory' while working with dataset's methods\" is not a frequent use case\n\nWith a crude search, these were the only examples I was able to locate in the codebase:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/744daa9993749bbfb756044dfaebb2d97df5b09a/datalad/interface/tests/test_save.py#L354-L362\n\nAnyway, while I don't prefer the ./path vs path distinction, I realize it's a very minor issue.  Feel free to close as \"not worth changing\"/\"feature\".","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1528209911,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NDczNjg3Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-394736873"},"message":"\u003e  So far I was under the impression that \"specify 'file in the current directory' while working with dataset's methods\" is not a frequent use case\n\nI guess as infrequent as adding a subdataset within a subdirectory, while being in that subdirectory. \nI guess workaround could be \"you have to specify full paths\" but it wouldn't scale if there are multiple entries.   I do feel that there were other, similar to `add` usecases mandating to use `-d .` or alike (`remove`?) but cannot recall since do not use them often.\nOverall -- I do think that ./path vs path distinction is ugly and not well documented and confusing.  But I fear that inability to work in command line within subdirectories (our tests really do not cover those use cases that often) without being able to specify current short paths would bite even more.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528210249,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NDczOTA2Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-394739067"},"message":"Now we are talking past each other. You were talking about \"dataset methods\" -- that is an invalid concept for the cmdline. I considered the \"./path vs path distinction\" a bug that I wanted to fix. However, if dataset methods shall start operating relative to the PWD and not relative to the dataset root this complicates the issue massively. So what is this bug about?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1558372887,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5NDA3NjkxNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2589#issuecomment-494076916"},"message":"With #3435, `save` would no longer treat \"./path\" and \"path\" differently when passed a dataset instance.  Closing this issue, because if gh-3435 is merged this can be considered fixed (at least in commands that don't use annotate_paths) and if it isn't merged this can be considered \"won't fix\".","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1558372887,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDIyNDc1NjMyMg=="},"target":"4cf7e33b19e4603453e09306a76f99afe62018f3bc613a7b84463172683b195f","message":"With #3435, `save` would no longer treat \"./path\" and \"path\" differently.  Closing this issue, because if gh-3435 is merged this can be considered fixed (at least in commands that don't use annotate_paths) and if it isn't merged this can be considered \"won't fix\".","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1558372859,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjM1Mzc5Njk0MQ=="},"status":2}]}